# Real-tool failure-tail corpus for the 31-pattern runtime diagnostics engine.
# Each block: a ``# intended=<pattern_id> exit=<code>`` header, blank-line
# separated, followed by a realistic multi-line stderr/stdout tail as a real
# failed rule emits it (tool banner/prelude + the decisive failure line +
# trailing shell/scheduler context). Every block is multi-line: the pattern's
# text appears *inside* surrounding tool output. For a few signals whose real
# signature genuinely IS one kernel/shell line (e.g. "Illegal instruction
# (core dumped)", "KeyboardInterrupt"), that decisive line is kept verbatim
# but is no longer the whole block: it is wrapped in the tool output that
# really surrounds it. A positive block MUST fire its intended pattern.
# See crates/oxo-flow-core/tests/diagnostic_corpus.rs.

